    "findings": [
      "Player bullets, shared summary rows, and per-variant pages match the verified target predicate, held-slot condition, tier values, ordinary stagger reset, and the separate active count_as_staggered alternative; the same hit that first staggers a previously unstaggered target does not gain the bonus retroactively.",
      "All five variants use I–IV +5%/+10%/+15%/+20% damage_vs_staggered; the bonus enters the additive damage-stat stage. The worked examples correctly show 100→120 and 130→150 for B=100, p=.20, q=0/.30, state assumptions, and do not present the result as a whole-hit multiplier or gameplay measurement.",
      "The finalized map, config, extension draft, seven UI bindings, five variant pages, and five reverse weapon pages agree on the five actual variants and seven marks; melee/ranged mixed classification and actual family/pattern/mark display names are consistent.",
      "Weapon action coverage distinguishes attack=0 pure melee pushes from damaging follow-ups; the Bolt Pistol variant page limits explosion claims to actual kill/stop/penetration-stop paths and explicitly excludes armor_explosion configuration; P4 Mk III special applies 3-second electrocuted while Mk VIII applies 8-second +0.25 rending; P2/P4 interval ticks require live owner stats and target-condition checks, with the documented P4 bomber skip.",
      "RAW English and zh-TW name/description strings and hashes are preserved; formatter reconstruction correctly maps each tier override to +5% through +20%, keeps the static reconstruction caveat, and treats zh-TW RAW “硬直” versus glossary “踉蹌” as a terminology difference rather than a mechanism erratum.",
      "The icon identity/path remains separate from the attachment URL, and its 128×128 image receipt has matching verified hash/display metadata.",
